    ("Ha Chong-Hyun: Conjunction", "Ha Chong-Hyun", 1981, "Oil on hemp cloth", "Korean Dansaekhwa", ["dansaekhwa","material","back-painting","hemp","minimal"], ["oil pushed through hemp","textured surface","material process","minimal"], ["ochre","grey through hemp texture"], "National Museum of Modern and Contemporary Art, Seoul", "Oil paint pushed through the back of hemp cloth, the texture of the fabric becoming the mark of the brush.", "Ha Chong-Hyun's back-pushing technique — painting through the canvas rather than on it — creates a unique material-process relationship.", "male", "Korean"),
